From: Hermes <hermes@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: increase GPU microcode reserved memory

The upstream sm8750.dtsi allocates only 8 KiB (0x2000) for GPU microcode,
but the Adreno 830 ZAP shader firmware (gen80000_zap.mbn) is ~12 KB in
MDT format which requires more memory for page-aligned segment loading.

Without sufficient reserved memory, zap_shader_load_mdt() fails silently,
the GPU stays in secure mode, and Vulkan/Gallium initialization fails
with "CP group not found", falling back to softpipe rendering.

Extend the region from 0x2000 to 0x6000 (24 KiB), which fits before the
adjacent spss region at 0x9b0a0000.

Signed-off-by: Hermes <hermes@localhost>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
@@ -452,7 +452,7 @@
 
 		gpu_micro_code_mem: gpu-micro-code@9b09a000 {
-			reg = <0x0 0x9b09a000 0x0 0x2000>;
+			reg = <0x0 0x9b09a000 0x0 0x6000>;
 			no-map;
 		};
